class:: TableMorph3D
summary:: Trilinear traversal of a prepared three-dimensional wavetable bank
categories:: UGens>Generators>Wavetable
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

TableMorph3D reads a row-major three-dimensional grid of equal-size
single-cycle tables. It trilinearly interpolates eight neighboring tables and
crossfades frequency-selected mip levels. TableMorph2D and TableMorph3D share
the same playback, interpolation, and mip-selection backend.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Osc::. Both read periodic tables, but
TableMorph3D traverses a prepared waveform volume and chooses bandlimited mip
levels automatically.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: bufnum
Mono Buffer returned by code::prepareBuffer::.

argument:: freq
Signed oscillator frequency in hertz.

argument:: x
Normalized x coordinate, clamped to code::0..1::.

argument:: y
Normalized y coordinate, clamped to code::0..1::.

argument:: z
Normalized z coordinate, clamped to code::0..1::.

argument:: phase
Readout phase offset in radians.

argument:: tablesX
Initialization-rate x dimension from code::1:: through code::128::.

argument:: tablesY
Initialization-rate y dimension from code::1:: through code::128::.

argument:: tablesZ
Initialization-rate z dimension from code::1:: through code::128::.

argument:: tableSize
Initialization-rate power-of-two table length from code::64:: through
code::65536::.

argument:: mipLevels
Initialization-rate prepared mip count from code::1:: through code::16::.

argument:: interpolation
Initialization-rate table interpolation: code::0:: nearest, code::1:: linear,
or code::2:: cubic.

argument:: mul
Output multiplier.

argument:: add
Offset added after multiplication.

returns::
One audio signal.

method:: kr

TableMorph3D is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

method:: prepareBuffer

argument:: server
Destination Server. Nil selects code::Server.default::.

argument:: tables
Flat row-major collection of finite samples in code::[z][y][x]:: order, with
x changing fastest.

argument:: tablesX
Literal x dimension from code::1:: through code::128::.

argument:: tablesY
Literal y dimension from code::1:: through code::128::.

argument:: tablesZ
Literal z dimension from code::1:: through code::128::.

argument:: mipLevels
Number of low-pass levels from code::1:: through code::16::.

argument:: normalize
Remove DC from every table and, when true, peak-normalize nonzero tables.

argument:: action
Function passed to the asynchronous Buffer loader.

returns::
The allocated Buffer with layout code::[mip][z][y][x][sample]::.

subsection:: Discussion

The declared dimensions must exactly match Buffer sample count. Freeing or
reallocating the Buffer permanently silences an active instance. Preparation
is asynchronous, so synchronize the server before playback.

examples::

code::
(
Routine({
    var size = 128;
    var tables = 8.collect { |index|
        Signal.sineFill(size, [1, index / 16, index / 32])
    };
    var buffer = TableMorph3D.prepareBuffer(
        s, tables, 2, 2, 2, 5
    );
    s.sync;
    {
        TableMorph3D.ar(
            buffer, 92,
            SinOsc.kr(0.07).range(0, 1),
            SinOsc.kr(0.09).range(0, 1),
            SinOsc.kr(0.11).range(0, 1),
            tablesX: 2, tablesY: 2, tablesZ: 2,
            tableSize: size, mipLevels: 5
        ) * 0.07
    }.play;
}).play;
)
::

code::
(
Routine({
    var size = 64;
    var tables = 27.collect { |index|
        Signal.sineFill(
            size, [1, (index % 3) / 6, index.div(3) / 30]
        )
    };
    var buffer = TableMorph3D.prepareBuffer(
        s, tables, 3, 3, 3, 4
    );
    s.sync;
    {
        TableMorph3D.ar(
            buffer, 61, 0.2, MouseX.kr(0, 1), MouseY.kr(0, 1),
            tablesX: 3, tablesY: 3, tablesZ: 3,
            tableSize: size, mipLevels: 4
        ) * 0.065
    }.play;
}).play;
)
::

